# Ticket test documentation

When you **complete**, **hand off**, or **close** work tied to a GitHub issue (or PR that fixes an issue), add a **Test plan** section so the next person can reproduce verification without re-deriving steps from the diff.

## Where to document

| Location | When |
|----------|------|
| **GitHub issue comment** | Default — post before close or with final PR link |
| **PR description** | Include the same checklist under `## Test plan` |
| **ADR / design doc** | Only for locked acceptance criteria — link issue; do not duplicate full play steps |

Do not mark an exploration/combat issue done without at least one **automated** or **manual** verification path recorded.

**Format:** Follow the **test-plan-grid-dungeon** agent skill (`.cursor/skills/test-plan-grid-dungeon/`) for full templates, step tables, N/A wording, and sign-off blocks. The short template below is a fallback only.

## Test plan template

```markdown
## Test plan (verified YYYY-MM-DD)

### Automated
- [ ] Unity Test Runner → Edit Mode → `Tests` → `<Domain>` → `<TestClass>` — all green (layout: [Assets/Tests/README.md](https://github.com/miramocha/griddungeon-game/blob/main/Assets/Tests/README.md); optional category filter e.g. `Combat`)
- [ ] (optional) Play Mode / CI — note job or N/A

### Manual (Play Mode)
- **Scene:** `DevBootstrap.unity` (local only — **GridDungeon → Scenes → Create Dev Bootstrap** after clone)
- **Setup:** `<F2 Exploration, InputRouter wired, …>`
- **Steps:**
  1. …
  2. …
- **Expected:** …

### Regressions checked
- [ ] …

### Spec / ADRs
- [ADR 001](../../decisions/001-grid-movement.md), [ADR 018](../../decisions/018-exploration-animation-speed.md), …
```

## Grid Dungeon defaults (exploration)

Unless the ticket changes timings, assume **Normal** preset (design-docs [ADR 018](../../decisions/018-exploration-animation-speed.md)): step **0.28s**, turn **0.26s**, hold-to-repeat per [ADR 001](../../decisions/001-grid-movement.md).

**Dev bootstrap:** `GridDungeon → Scenes → Create Dev Bootstrap` if scene refs are stale; **F1** Hub / **F2** Exploration / **F3** Combat (dev fight: 2 cores + slime when roster empty — see game repo `Assets/Scripts/README.md`). **F3 QA:** core command turns highlight **party roster**, not AGI strip ([combat.md](../../docs/02-systems/combat.md#turn-order-strip-agi-queue-ui)).

